    "s1": {
      "x": 1700,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 460,
      "fill": "orange",
      "text": "Built on the founders' own logo, colours and deck imagery.\n\nThe moon mark is a moon, a padel ball (seam) and a racket face (holes). The campaign shows it in phases: crescent to tease, half to announce, gibbous for hype, full moon on match night.\n\nColour from the logo: Space, Night, Court, Electric, Ice, Silver. Medal gold for winners only.\n\nType: Montserrat, the closest open match to the wordmark.\n\nDeck images are 1,240px renders; swap in high-res files and real footage when available."
    },
    "t2": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": 2120,
      "text": "Days 1 to 3 \u00b7 Moon-phase teasers, as they sit on the grid",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 3400
    },
    "s2": {
      "x": 3500,
      "y": 2420,
      "w": 460,
      "fill": "blue",
      "text": "Post order: right tile on Day 1, middle on Day 2, left on Day 3.\n\nThe moon mark waxes from crescent to full, and the court goes from dim lines to fully lit on Day 3.\n\nOnly three feed posts follow (Days 4, 5, 7), so this row stays intact. Day 6 runs in Stories.\n\nAll feed posts are 1080 x 1440 (3:4)."
    },
